course: dictionary
lesson: 15374
title: Using words sparingly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Sparingly» means using only a little of something, and using it carefully so that none is wasted. It is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done. Look for the clue in the word «use»: you are told to use less than you might.
explain: «Use the salt sparingly.» In a recipe this means add only a pinch, not a big spoonful. «Put the glue on sparingly» means a small dab, so the card does not get soggy and the glue lasts.
explain: Sparingly is the opposite of using something lavishly, which means using plenty of it. When you meet a new word, ask: is the text telling me to use a lot or a little? The words around it give you the answer.
fact: Sparingly means using only a little of something, carefully and not wastefully.
fact: Sparingly is an adverb: it tells you how something is done, as in «use it sparingly».
fact: «Use the salt sparingly» means add only a pinch.
fact: In a drought, people use water sparingly so there is enough for everyone.
fact: The food pyramid says to eat sugary foods sparingly, because too many is not healthy.
exercise: «Dad told us to use the shampoo sparingly.» What does sparingly mean? | Using it very fast | *Using only a little, carefully | Throwing it away after one use | Using as much as you can
exercise: «The farmer waters the crops sparingly in the dry summer.» What does the farmer do? | Floods the fields every day | *Uses only a little water, carefully | Stops watering the crops completely | Waters the crops at midnight
exercise: Ella says, «Eat sweets sparingly.» What does she mean? | Eat them all before dinner | Eat as many as you like | *Only a little at a time | Never eat them at all, not even one
test: «The artist painted the sky sparingly, with just a few dabs of blue.» What does sparingly mean here? | Painting very loudly | Painting without any colour at all | Using lots of paint everywhere | *Using only a little paint, carefully
test: «In a drought, people use water sparingly.» Why do they do this? | *To save it, so there is enough | Because water is free and they have plenty | To wash the car every day | To make the garden flood
exam: Which word means using only a little of something, carefully and not wastefully? | *Sparingly | Loudly | Lavishly | Angrily
